        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "40d14c8a-d5c8-539b-b5e9-f315b199105a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Battle of Okinawa, Operation Diadem, Operation Strangle\n- People: Dave Schreiner\n- Organizations: United States Marine Corps, United States Army, Imperial Japanese Army, U.S. Fifth Army, British Eighth Army, Allies of World War II\n- Places: Okinawa, Monte Cassino, Liri Valley, Italy\n\nFacts:\n- In May 1944, the Allies of World War II launched Operation Diadem, an offensive in the Italian Campaign carried out by the U.S. Fifth Army and British Eighth Army.\n- Operation Diadem was also known as the Fourth Battle of Monte Cassino and, in Canada, as the Battle of the Liri Valley.\n- Operation Strangle did not achieve its initial goal of forcing the enemy to withdraw, but its air interdiction contributed significantly to the success of the subsequent ground assault, Operation Diadem.\n- On April 1, 1945, the Battle of Okinawa began with the invasion of Okinawa under the codename Operation Iceberg.\n- The Battle of Okinawa was a major Pacific War battle in which United States Marine and Army forces fought the Imperial Japanese Army on Okinawa.\n- The Battle of Okinawa included the largest amphibious assault of the Pacific War during World War II.\n- Dave Schreiner was mortally wounded while serving as a Marine on June 20, 1945, during the Battle of Okinawa.\n- Dave Schreiner died on June 21, 1945, one day after being mortally wounded in the Battle of Okinawa.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "0ea78eba-0e20-5b94-b521-de36bb1f78f4",
        "text": "Page: Battle of Okinawa. Sentence: The Battle of Okinawa (Japanese: 沖縄戦 , Hepburn: Okinawa-sen ) (Okinawan: 沖縄戦 , \"Uchinaa ikusa \" ), codenamed Operation Iceberg, was a major battle of the Pacific War fought on the island of Okinawa by United States Marine and Army forces against the Imperial Japanese Army and included the largest amphibious assault in the Pacific War during World War II, the April 1, 1945, invasion of Okinawa itself.\nPage: Operation Diadem. Sentence: Operation Diadem, also referred to as the Fourth Battle of Monte Cassino or, in Canada, the Battle of the Liri Valley, was an offensive operation undertaken by the Allies of World War II (U.S. Fifth Army and British Eighth Army in May 1944, as part of the Italian Campaign of World War II.\nPage: Dave Schreiner. Sentence: He was mortally wounded in action as a Marine on June 20, 1945 during the Battle of Okinawa and died the next day.\nPage: Operation Strangle (World War II). Sentence: Although the initial goal of forcing the enemy to withdraw was not achieved, the air interdiction of Operation Strangle played a major role in the success of the subsequent ground assault Operation \"Diadem\".",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
